„­bible_version£KJV¤book'§chapter¨sections–…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAnd it came to pass, when Jesus had made an end of commanding his twelve disciples, he departed thence to teach and to preach in their cities.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙXNow when John had heard in the prison the works of Christ, he sent two of his disciples,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙKand said unto him, Art thou he that should come, or do we look for another?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ`Jesus answered and said unto them, Go and shew John again those things which ye do hear and see:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¤the blind receive their sight, and the lame walk, the lepers are cleansed, and the deaf hear, the dead are raised up, and the poor have the gospel preached to them.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ9And blessed is he, whosoever shall not be offended in me.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses™„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ—And as they departed, Jesus began to say unto the multitudes concerning John, What went ye out into the wilderness to see? A reed shaken with the wind?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙzBut what went ye out for to see? A man clothed in soft raiment? behold, they that wear soft clothing are in kings' houses.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙYBut what went ye out for to see? A prophet? yea, I say unto you, and more than a prophet.¦layout ªlast_verse	„¥verse
